    "wa-bingen": {
      "facingDeg": 180,
      "windArcHalfWidthDeg": 90,
      "windMinMph": 5,
      "windMaxMph": 15,
      "gustMaxMph": 20,
      "region": "Washington",
      "notes": "South and west launches above a grass LZ at Bingen Marina; 2,100 ft descent. Best in sunny, calm conditions or light east/west winds under 10 mph. Good thermal days: 2,500 ft gains and eastward XC potential. Westerlies favor the intermediate west launch. East winds can be rough and unpredictable, with crosswinds and tumbling air at south launch. High-wind hazards: whitecaps, dull water streaks and a wind line approaching from the west. Whitecaps at the marina or an approaching west wind line indicate blown-out conditions. Visit the LZ first; winds there can be stronger. In wind, launch only if kiting at the LZ is manageable. Park across from the log cabin. Follow the trail downhill, then uphill around the private property; the detour adds about 1 min. Stay on the trail and close and latch the cattle gate. South launch: 5–10 min walk, flat area west of a lone oak; east or south winds only, usually east. West launch: 15 min farther along the trail; spring thermal and ridge soaring.",
      "countryCode": "US"
    },
